---
description: Colocate helpers in the owning file; do not add a file per function
alwaysApply: true
---

# File colocation

A new source file is allowed only when one of these is true:

- It is a real boundary: route, service, repository, model, worker handler, React
  component, or React hook (one component/hook per file stays).
- The same non-trivial logic is used by two or more other files, and those files
  should not each own a copy.

Otherwise the function goes in the file that calls it, or in the existing file
that already owns that concern. Do not add a file that nothing in production
calls. Do not copy the same helper under a new name.

Prefer fewer modules/folders when two folders are the same concern.

## Line cap (code only)

A file must not exceed **1000 code lines**. Do not count blank lines, `//` comments,
or `/* */` / JSDoc blocks.

If a file would go over 1000 code lines, **do not create a new file**. Move the extra
concern into another **existing** file that already owns related work. Only add a
file if no existing owner can take it without mixing unrelated concerns.

```js
// BAD — one unused helper, own file
// organizationScope.js
export function assertOrganizationPathMatchesPrincipal(pathOrgId, principal) {
  if (String(pathOrgId) !== String(principal.orgId)) {
    throw ApiError.fromCode('NOT_FOUND');
  }
}

// GOOD — live in the caller or the file that already owns the concern
export function createAuthorizePreHandler(requiredPermissions) {
  return async function authorize(request) {
    if (String(request.params.orgId) !== String(request.principal.orgId)) {
      throw ApiError.fromCode('NOT_FOUND');
    }
  };
}
```
